---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/foce/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Bonus Project: Simon Says</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">Optional &mdash; Extra Credit</h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            The board plays a sequence of lights and tones. You repeat it back on
            the buttons. Every round it adds one more step, and it gets away from
            you faster than you expect.
          </p>

          <p>
            This is the hardest of the bonus projects and the one most worth
            doing. Everything it needs you already have &mdash; a list that grows,
            buttons that get read, LEDs and a speaker. Nothing new, just more of
            it at once.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="needs">
          <h2>What You&#39;ll Need</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Four LEDs, each with its own resistor</li>
            <li>Four buttons, each from <code>3V3</code> to its own pin with <code>Pin.PULL_DOWN</code></li>
            <li>The speaker, through its 330&#8486; resistor</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Four buttons is exactly what the kit contains. Give each LED a
            different tone &mdash; that is what makes the sequence memorable
            rather than just visible.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="tasks">
          <h2>Build It</h2>

          <ol>
            <li><b>Wire four of each</b> and prove all eight parts work before writing any game logic. A dead button discovered mid-game is very hard to spot.</li>
            <li><b>Play one step.</b> Pick a random light, flash it with its tone, then wait for a press. Right button or wrong?</li>
            <li><b>Grow a list.</b> Keep the sequence in a list and <code>append()</code> a new random step each round.</li>
            <li><b>Play the whole sequence back</b> each round, from the start, before the player&#39;s turn.</li>
            <li><b>Check the player&#39;s presses in order.</b> One wrong press ends the game.</li>
            <li><b>Report the score</b> &mdash; how many rounds they survived.</li>
          </ol>

          <p>
            The trick in task 5 is comparing two things that arrive at different
            times: the sequence is already in a list, and the presses come in one
            at a time. Compare each press against the sequence position it should
            match, and stop at the first mismatch.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>What Success Looks Like</h2>

          <pre class="bg-sn-darker p-3 rounded"><code>Round 1 &mdash; watch...  your turn  OK
Round 2 &mdash; watch...  your turn  OK
Round 3 &mdash; watch...  your turn  wrong!

You made it to round 3.</code></pre>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="extend">
          <h2>Then Make It Yours</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Speed the playback up as the sequence grows</li>
            <li>Let the player choose a difficulty at the start</li>
            <li>Show the round number on the OLED</li>
            <li>Play a distinct losing sound rather than just stopping</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Project
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
